        "status": "confirmed",
        "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions and are mathematically correct. q-48504: the quotient rule gives x(2 ln x−1)/(ln x)^2, which equals e at x=e. q-11969: the quotient-rule numerator is −9. q-4807: the slope is 5, so y−3=5(x−1). q-103325: the slope at x=1 is 3, giving y=3x−9 and intersection (3,0). Its source writes “m={f}^{′}(-1)=12(1)^{2}-9=3.” The evaluation label should be f′(1); this authored notation inconsistency does not change the answer because f′(−1)=f′(1)=3. q-84959 and q-122560: unordered selections give binomial coefficients C(9,4)=126 and C(12,3)=220. All eight graphs have period 2π: q-118350 and q-6580 are negative sine with amplitudes 1/4 and 1; q-6761 and q-12675 are negative cosine with amplitudes 1 and 1.5; q-118442 and q-118443 are negative sine with amplitudes 5 and 6, equivalently 5 sin(−x) and 6 sin(−x) because sine is odd; q-118450 and q-68373 are negative sine shifted down 1 and 4. Parentheses around x in the selected sine/cosine choices do not change the source expressions. Finally, the product rule gives 2e+e=3e for q-48835 and −3/4−2=−11/4 for q-48836. Confirmation is based on the supplied worked solutions; no captured grade is supplied.",
